WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.490
- Donald Trump's law firm,

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:04.700
and by that I of course mean
the US Justice Department,

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.227
is suing to block the
publication of John Bolton's book

00:00:07.227 --> 00:00:08.950
"The Room Where it Happened."

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.230
Yes for the title of the book,

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.080
Bolton and his publisher
ripped off the lyrics

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.420
from the musical Hamilton.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.930
Whereas Hamilton tells the inspiring story

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:17.110
of the founding of America,

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:18.450
Bolton's book tells the tale

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.250
of a mustachioed government official

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.320
who has damning information

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.010
about the President of the United States,

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.820
but writes a book instead of testifying

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.660
at the president's impeachment trial.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:27.810
Now with a book being released,

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.870
President Trump is calling Bolton names

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.240
while Bolton is doing dumb things

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.880
that will probably make it
impossible for him to get paid

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.150
from proceeds of the book.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:37.473
- There really isn't any guiding principle

00:00:37.473 --> 00:00:40.650
that I was able to discern
other than what's good

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.360
for Donald Trump's reelection.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.250
- Which makes one wonder
why he didn't testify

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.760
in the impeachment trial at all,

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.530
and instead waited to put
it all into a book itself.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.160
There are no heroes here in the story,

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.670
but there are important questions

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.250
at the heart of this dispute.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.180
Did Bolton willfully disclose
classified information

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:00.320
that could compromise national security?

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.700
Or did the Trump administration

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.290
abuse the classification process

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:05.250
to protect Trump's personal interests?

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.430
Or is the answer both?

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.820
We simply don't know exactly what happens

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.780
during the pre-publication
review process of Bolton's book.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.850
And as I explained in another video,

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.820
that's exactly why Legal
Eagle has filed a FOIA request

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.040
for information about the
pre-publication review

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:20.880
of Bolton's book,

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.430
and that's also why I'm filing
suit against the White House.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.720
Because the public has a
right to know what happened

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:28.580
and we hope to shed some light on it

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.410
through the public records requests.

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:33.080
But in this video, I wanna
break down the DOJ's lawsuit

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:35.020
and the motion it filed for an injunction

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.350
to stop publication of John Bolton's book.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.970
And I'll also let you in on a big secret.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:42.050
I also filed a petition
asking the government

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:43.243
to declassify all of the things

00:01:43.243 --> 00:01:45.973
they just told the court
our government secrets.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.720
Hey Legal Eagles, it's
time to think like a lawyer

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.227
because John Bolton is
trying to tell his story

00:01:55.227 --> 00:01:57.830
and the government is trying to stop him.

00:01:57.830 --> 00:02:00.770
The first legal question
posed by the DOJ's lawsuit

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:01.860
is whether John Bolton

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.870
violated his non-disclosure agreements

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.500
by disclosing classified
and sensitive information.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.920
The government wants two
things from this lawsuit.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.740
Number one, it wants an injunction

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:13.527
against the planned June 23rd
publication of Bolton's book

00:02:13.527 --> 00:02:15.820
"The Room Where it Happened:
A White House Memoir".

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.920
And two, a constructive trust

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:19.290
that would give the
United States the right

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:22.060
to all of Bolton's profits from this book.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.280
So let's break this down piece by piece.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.410
First, let's talk about the NDAs,

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:28.170
the non disclosure agreements.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.670
The government is suing
Bolton for breach of contract.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:31.630
According to the complaint,

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.420
the contracts in question are
non-disclosure agreements,

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.640
otherwise known as NDAs

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.600
that Bolton signed on April 5th 2018,

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:39.910
when he entered government service

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.330
as the National Security Advisor.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:43.700
Despite what you may have read,

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.770
it's not unusual for
National Security employees

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:47.060
to sign NDAs.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.380
In fact, it's generally required.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.010
The government started requiring employees

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.750
to sign secrecy agreements in 1947.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.210
Today, every US intelligence agency

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:58.950
imposes a lifetime
pre-publication review requirement

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.330
on at least some subset
of former employees.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.370
The agreements have generally
prohibited employees

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.570
from publishing manuscripts

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:08.330
without first obtaining
the agency's consent.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.410
In 1988, divided Supreme Court

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.330
decided Snepp versus United States

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.920
which affirmed the imposition
of a constructive trust

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.840
on proceeds earned by a former CIA officer

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.820
who would publish the book
without submitting it for review.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:23.320
So when a former employee
wants to write a book,

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:25.400
they have to go through
this pre-publication review.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.220
They have to give the
manuscript to the government

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.500
so that they can review it

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.850
for potentially sensitive
or classified information.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:33.530
And when a person secures
pre-publication clearance,

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:35.660
he or she can publish without liability

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.690
and keep all the profits from that book.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:38.670
But in a situation

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:41.180
where someone like Bolton
publishes without clearance,

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.520
the government can ask

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:45.000
that the courts establish
a constructive trust,

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.210
meaning that the government
gets all of the money

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:50.270
that the person would have made
because of the publication.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:51.770
Bolton signed two agreements

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:53.770
which are now the subject of this lawsuit.

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:56.350
In the first NDA, Standard Form 312,

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.550
Bolton agreed that he must never quote,

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:01.420
divulge classified information
to anyone, end quote,

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.970
unless he either quote,
officially verifies

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.240
that the recipient has
been properly authorized

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.180
by the United States
government to receive it,

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:11.270
or he's received prior written
notice of authorization

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.530
to divulge it from the
United States government.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.780
Specifically the entity responsible for

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.340
that information's classification,

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:18.610
which sometimes can get dicey

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.460
when you have people in
different departments,

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.830
all of those different departments

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:25.060
may have to conduct some sort
of pre-publication review.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.210
And generally speaking,

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:29.380
that means that the employee
needs permission first.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:32.780
The second NDA, Form 4414,
covers Bolton's access

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:35.710
to a more sensitive subset
of classified information,

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:38.470
commonly known as sensitive
compartmented information

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:39.670
or SCI.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.970
You can imagine that as the
National Security Advisor,

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.120
Bolton had access

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:45.830
to the most sensitive government
information available.

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.750
The terms of his NDA require Bolton

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.540
to submit to a security review

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.060
by the National Security Council,

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.280
any writing that contains SCI

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:55.430
or activities that relate to SCI.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:57.970
Bolton also agreed that he would quote,

00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:00.980
not disclose the contents
of any SCI-related material

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:03.760
with anyone who is not
authorized to have access to it

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:06.720
until he received written
authorization from the quote,

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:10.600
department or agency that last
authorized my access to SCI

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.710
that such disclosure is permitted.

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:14.290
Okay, so now that we know Bolton

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.170
has to go through this
pre-publication review

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.630
before he can disclose
anything that is classified

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:22.180
or that is SCI or even
related to SCI to anyone,

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:24.710
what did he do with his manuscript?

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:28.740
Well, when Bolton left his
employment in September of 2019,

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:30.420
he wrote a manuscript

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:33.140
which he believed did not
contain classified information.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:34.930
On December 30th 2019,

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:36.720
Bolton's lawyer submitted the manuscript

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.320
for pre-publication review.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.280
The manuscript was sent to Ellen Knight,

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:42.560
the NSC Senior Director for Records Access

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:44.220
and Information Security Management.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.330
This is the NSC entity

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:49.230
that usually does classification
and pre-publication reviews

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:51.010
for the National Security Council.

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:51.930
Less than a month later,

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.960
Knight sent the manuscript back to Bolton

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:55.670
having identified a number of things

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:58.100
that she claimed were classified.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.850
This started a three-month
process between Bolton and Knight

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:02.660
in which they negotiated
many of the changes

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.550
to the manuscript in order to
assure that in Knight's view,

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.990
it wouldn't contain any
classified information.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:09.000
And one of the quirks

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.810
about the pre-publication review process

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:12.740
is that you're technically
not even allowed

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:14.870
to show the manuscript to your lawyer.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:17.300
I mean, you can but
you're not supposed to,

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.130
they don't have the
same kind of clearances,

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:21.610
and you can get in big
trouble if the lawyer

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.080
is the one that's negotiating
it instead of the client.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:27.060
So often, these people are
completely unrepresented,

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:29.840
as they are going back and
forth in negotiating things

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:30.880
with the government.

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.230
And in this case, Bolton
and Knight met several times

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:35.040
and also corresponded in writing.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.840
By April 27 2020,

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:38.900
Knight quote, had completed her review

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:41.720
and was of the judgment
that the manuscript draft

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:44.280
did not contain classified information.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.690
Knight told Bolton her review was final

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:47.940
and all they were waiting for

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.210
was the official letter confirming the end

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:51.838
of the pre-publication review.

00:06:51.838 --> 00:06:54.450
But then the current
National Security Advisor,

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.570
Robert O'Brien became concerned

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:59.430
that the manuscripts still
contain classified information

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:01.010
even after Knight's review.

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:03.170
O'Brien allegedly asked Michael Ellis,

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:05.520
the NSC's Senior Director
for Intelligence,

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.120
to do another review of the manuscript.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:11.320
Unlike Knight, Ellis is
a political appointee.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:14.040
Ellis was also allegedly
involved in the decision

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:17.940
to classify President
Trump's July 25th 2019 call

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:20.320
with Ukrainian President
Volodymyr Zelensky

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:23.140
in the White House's most secure
classified computer system.

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:26.560
Remember that whole thing
about the Ukrainian scandal?

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:30.720
Apparently Ellis was involved
in potentially corrupt action

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.222
to hide the transcript of that call

00:07:33.222 --> 00:07:35.920
with other members of the administration.

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.530
It feels like a lot
has happened since then

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:41.410
but you might recall that
that call with Zelensky

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:42.530
later became an issue

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:44.360
in President Trump's impeachment trial.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.160
At any rate, by June 8th, the
government had reversed course

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:47.993
and informed Bolton

00:07:47.993 --> 00:07:50.990
that the manuscripts still
contain classified information.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.230
But the government did not
identify the information

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:55.470
that it contended was secret.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:58.070
On June 10th, Bolton's
lawyer told the government

00:07:58.070 --> 00:07:59.230
that in Bolton's opinion,

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:01.427
it did not continue any
prohibited information

00:08:01.427 --> 00:08:03.190
and that the book had been printed

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:04.670
and shipped to distributors.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:08.300
On June 16th 2020, the NSC
sent Bolton a marked copy

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.700
of the current version of the manuscript

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:12.280
identifying passages that
Ellis thought appeared

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:14.170
to contain classified information.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:15.750
The book as of the time of this video,

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:18.700
was scheduled for publication
on June 23th 2020.

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:22.110
So given that John Bolton is
trying to publish his book

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:25.370
before the end of the
pre-publication review process,

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:28.980
whether that process was
conducted in good faith or not,

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.290
it's not surprising that
the Department of Justice

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:34.480
is suing Bolton for
breaching the two NDAs.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:37.100
And the government is asking
for four kinds of relief.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.560
Number one, enjoining
Bolton from taking any steps

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.820
towards publicly
disclosing the information

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:42.890
in "The Room Where it Happened"

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:45.180
without first obtaining
written permission.

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:47.720
Two, requiring Bolton to delay publication

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.200
and instruct his publisher to do the same.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.430
Three, imposing a constructive trust

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:54.050
that would give the
United States the right

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:56.780
to all the profits that
Bolton gets from his book.

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:58.820
And four, declaring that the court's order

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:00.560
prohibiting disclosure of the information

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.580
will bind the publisher, Simon &amp; Schuster,

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:05.340
and any other party in the
commercial distribution chain,

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:07.940
even if they aren't actually
named in the lawsuit.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:11.600
Now, violating an NDA creates
a breach of contract claim,

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:12.900
and a breach of contract claim

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:15.910
in the national security context
is a lot more complicated

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:18.250
than when a company sues an ex-employee

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.680
for violating an NDA.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:22.560
But what they do have in
common is the need to determine

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.930
what information is within
the scope of the agreement.

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:26.910
The government has the burden of proving

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:28.500
that the book contains information

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.240
that was within the scope of the NDA.

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:32.250
And pre-publication review covers more

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:34.080
than just classified information.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:36.620
Many agencies require
unclassified information

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:37.780
to be redacted as well.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:39.550
And since the National Security Council

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.380
just does this on an ad hoc basis,

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:42.620
there's no reason to believe

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:44.460
that they limited their redactions

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:46.360
to simply classified information,

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:48.480
so who knows what they
required John Bolton

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:49.840
to remove from his book.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:52.790
But under Executive Order 13526,

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:56.240
what is covered by the NDA
is incredibly expansive.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:58.560
Under Section 1.1, the
government must show

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.870
that the unauthorized
disclosure of information

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:01.970
in Bolton's book,

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:04.700
quote reasonably could be
expected to result in damage

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:07.030
to the national security, end quote.

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:08.410
This means that the government must prove

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:11.230
that the information has
been properly classified.

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:12.740
And the term national security

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:14.820
is defined to include the national defense

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:17.070
or foreign relations of the United States.

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:18.920
This is a pretty vague term

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:20.910
that could encompass almost anything

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:22.880
and the court in the Bolton case will need

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:25.270
to review the information
to determine if the agency

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:29.040
was acting in good faith when
it classified that material.

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:30.580
But according to a case

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:32.220
from the Fourth Circuit Court of Appeals,

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:34.340
a court will give
deference to the government

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:37.210
but at the same time, it
has to review the material

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:40.210
to ensure that the reviewing
agency had a good reason

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:42.930
to classify that particular information.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:44.190
The court observed in that case

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:45.560
that courts should require

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:48.610
that agency explanations
justify censorship

00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:50.550
with reasonable specificity,

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:52.300
demonstrating a logical connection

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:53.640
between the deleted information

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:56.040
and the reasons for classification.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:58.890
They should not rely on a
presumption of regularity

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:01.460
if such rational explanations are missing.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:04.450
The court anticipated that in
camera review of affidavits,

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:07.300
followed if necessary by
further judicial inquiry,

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:08.390
will be the norm.

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.070
Courts must assure themselves

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:11.630
that the reasons for classification

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:13.630
are rational and plausible ones.

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:15.320
And in a footnote to that decision,

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.410
the court suggested that
the government may be held

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:20.920
to a higher standard if an
agency seeks an injunction

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:23.000
against publication of the censored items.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:23.850
For better or worse,

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:26.790
no court has considered
the injunction issue yet

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.200
and generally speaking,

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:31.810
courts are loath to give what's
called a prior restraint,

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:34.930
where the government prevents
speech from being made

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:36.400
before that speech has made.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:38.730
That generally carries
with it the highest burden

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:39.830
under the First Amendment.

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:42.680
But can the government prove
that it made a rational

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:46.600
and plausible classification
decision in Bolton's case?

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:47.570
It's possible.

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:49.190
The biggest factor against the government

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:51.280
is that Knight told Bolton

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:53.880
that the book did not
contain classified material.

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:55.110
However, at that time,

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:57.660
he hadn't received final
clearance for publication

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:59.790
and sometimes government employees,

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:00.970
sometimes even the same ones,

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:02.880
change their mind about these things.

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:05.830
And so let's look to the
actual terms of the NDAs

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:07.910
that Bolton agreed to sign on to.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:11.730
When Bolton signed Form 312,
he agreed that he was uncertain

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:14.090
about the classification
status of any information

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:14.923
and therefore,

00:12:14.923 --> 00:12:17.210
he must get agency clearance
before disclosing it.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.680
Bolton will argue that
he was not uncertain

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:23.120
about the classification status
of the material in his book.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:25.320
Number one, because he knows the material,

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:28.270
number two, he got the
green light from Knight.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:30.210
However, this presents
a problem for Bolton

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:32.610
because the government
alleges that Bolton is the one

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:34.830
who decided to classify
some of the material

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:36.810
that he now discloses in his book.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.530
It's possible that Bolton will argue

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:40.430
that he actually improperly classified

00:12:40.430 --> 00:12:41.320
some of that information

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.790
which of course makes him look pretty bad.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:45.200
But if the government is correct,

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.720
then Bolton breached his
obligations under Form 312,

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:48.890
not to disclose material

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:51.210
without pre-publication
review and authorization.

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:52.197
But it's also possible

00:12:52.197 --> 00:12:54.660
that the pre-publication review process

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:58.030
was a complete sham done
by political appointees

00:12:58.030 --> 00:13:00.330
for political reasons to punish Bolton

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:02.910
as opposed to protecting the disclosure

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:04.950
of actually classified information.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:09.230
But turning to Form 4414,
Section Five of the NDA states,

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:10.470
I understand that the purpose

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.130
of the review described in paragraph four

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:14.890
is to give the United States
a reasonable opportunity

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:17.440
to determine whether the
preparation submitted pursuant

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:20.020
to paragraph four sets forth any SCI.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:22.850
He also must get
pre-clearance of any writing

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:25.830
that describes activities
that relate to SCI.

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:28.130
Since Bolton did not get
written authorization

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:28.963
before publishing,

00:13:28.963 --> 00:13:31.780
the government has a good
argument for constructive trust.

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:34.560
And constructive trust
is a lot easier to get

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:38.790
instead of actually censorship
of the material itself.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.900
It's a lot easier for the
government simply to punish people

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:42.550
for disclosing the information

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:44.970
than it is to prevent that
information from getting out

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:46.230
in the first place.

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:49.800
So that takes us to the
government's emergency motion.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:52.130
The second legal question in this case

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:55.530
is whether President Trump
can stop Bolton's book

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:56.850
from being published.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:59.680
The DOJ filed an emergency
motion for an injunction

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:01.670
against publication of the Bolton book

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:04.170
on the basis that it contains
classified information,

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:06.770
this is otherwise known as a
temporary restraining order.

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:09.280
Tellingly, the lawsuit
was filed against Bolton

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:11.680
and not the publisher of
the book Simon &amp; Schuster.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:13.370
But the government cites

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:15.890
Federal Rule of Civil Procedure 65d,

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:18.970
which states that an injunction
binds not only the parties,

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:21.840
but also the officers,
agents, servants, employees

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:24.600
and attorneys and all the
persons who are in contact

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:26.800
into actual notice of the injunction.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.660
The DOJ contends that if the
court grants the injunction,

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:31.270
that it should also bind the publishers

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:32.500
and ultimately the booksellers,

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:35.220
and probably everyone else
including journalists as well.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:38.070
So let's talk about the
law of prior restraint

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:40.788
because this is coming up fairly often.

00:14:40.788 --> 00:14:43.950
In First Amendment law, prior
restraint is government action

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:45.960
that prohibits speech and other expression

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:48.070
before the speech actually happens.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:49.810
It's considered the most serious form

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:50.800
of government censorship

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:52.970
and therefore the government
bears a heavy burden

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:55.530
when it seeks to stop
something from being published.

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:56.470
And at first glance,

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:58.130
the motion here appears to be based

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:00.500
on the standards set forth
in the Pentagon Papers case

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.130
which played a role in Watergate,

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.780
and I've covered that case
many times on this channel.

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:07.320
But in quick summary, the
Pentagon Papers was the name given

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:09.300
to a top secret Department
of Defense study

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:12.310
of the US political and
military involvement in Vietnam

00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:14.730
from 1945 to 1967.

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:17.290
The government military
analyst, Daniel Ellsberg,

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:20.060
who had worked on the study
came to oppose the war

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.920
and decided that the information contained

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:23.430
in the Pentagon Papers should be available

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:24.530
to the American public.

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:28.070
So he photocopied the
report and in March of 1971,

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:31.202
gave a copy of the Pentagon
Papers to the New York Times,

00:15:31.202 --> 00:15:34.210
which then published a
series of scathing articles

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:35.870
based on the contents.

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:37.080
The Pentagon Papers showed

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:39.140
that the Vietnam War was unwinnable

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:41.950
and that Nixon, Johnson,
Kennedy, Eisenhower and Truman

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:45.180
had all misled the public about
America's role in Vietnam.

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:48.090
In that case, the DOJ sued
to stop further publication

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:49.890
of the classified material.

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:51.980
But the Washington Post
and the New York Times

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:54.960
fought the DOJ and Supreme
Court ruled that the government

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:57.490
had failed to prove harm
to national security,

00:15:57.490 --> 00:15:59.720
and that publication of
the papers was justified

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:00.980
under the First Amendment's

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:02.680
protection of freedom of the press.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:03.513
In that case,

00:16:03.513 --> 00:16:05.560
the government could not
overcome the heavy presumption

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.580
against prior restraint of the press.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:09.300
And justices Black and Douglas

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:12.210
argued that the vague word
security should not be used

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:14.300
to abrogate the fundamental law embodied

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:15.310
in the First Amendment.

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:16.297
And the Supreme Court stated,

00:16:16.297 --> 00:16:18.397
"The guarding of military
and diplomatic secrets

00:16:18.397 --> 00:16:21.137
"at the expense of informed
representative government

00:16:21.137 --> 00:16:23.977
"provides no real
security for our republic.

00:16:23.977 --> 00:16:25.987
"The framers of the First
Amendment fully aware

00:16:25.987 --> 00:16:29.197
"of both the need to defend a new nation

00:16:29.197 --> 00:16:32.247
"and the abuses of the English
and colonial governments

00:16:32.247 --> 00:16:35.847
"sought to give this new
society strength and security

00:16:35.847 --> 00:16:38.967
"by providing that freedom
of speech, press, religion

00:16:38.967 --> 00:16:41.750
"and assembly should not be abridged."

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:44.400
And because of those
principles and that language,

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.170
there's only been one significant example

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:48.080
of a successful government injunction,

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:51.360
and that was in 1979, where
the US Department of Energy

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:54.890
sued The Progressive magazine
to prevent an article written

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:58.490
by an activist that revealed
how to make a hydrogen bomb.

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:00.050
Although the government did not allege

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:02.560
that the article posed
immediate or inevitable danger,

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:04.380
the Department of Energy
did say that the article

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:07.200
would increase the risk of
thermonuclear proliferation.

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:09.510
And that was enough
for a US District Court

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:12.010
to find that the security
of the US and the world

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:13.720
would be at risk, stating that,

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.580
a mistake in ruling
against the United States

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:19.040
could pave the way for
thermonuclear Armageddon for us all.

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:21.700
In that event, our right
to life is extinguished

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:23.830
and the right to publish becomes moot.

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:26.730
And therefore, publication
could indeed cause quote,

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:29.137
grave, direct, immediate
and irreparable harm

00:17:29.137 --> 00:17:30.760
to the United States.

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:33.600
Thereby meeting the test, the
Supreme Court had enunciated

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:35.193
in the Pentagon Papers case.

00:17:35.193 --> 00:17:37.320
And although the government
got its injunction

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.330
at the district court
level, the trial court,

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:40.940
it abandoned the case when it appealed

00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:42.680
because it turns out the information

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:46.100
about how to build an
H-bomb was already known

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:47.460
and widely disseminated.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.160
And so if there was no secret,

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.550
then there was no reason
for the censorship.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:53.700
So does anything in Bolton's book rise

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:55.910
to the level of national security secret

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:57.770
established by the Pentagon Papers case

00:17:57.770 --> 00:17:59.640
or the hydrogen bomb case?

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.550
Well, the government says yes, quote,

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:03.770
unlike ordinary confidential information

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:06.100
the government holds, the
information at stake here

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:08.380
is classified including some instances

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:11.010
at the secret or top secret SCI levels,

00:18:11.010 --> 00:18:12.300
which means by definition

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:14.580
that its disclosure
reasonably could be expected

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:18.120
to cause serious damage or
exceptionally grave damage

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:20.700
to the national security
of the United States.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.770
That comes from the Ellis Declaration

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:24.490
sworn under penalty of perjury

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:26.210
that was filed with the court.

00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:28.950
And in Mr. Ellis's
judgment, certain passages,

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:30.210
if disclosed, quote,

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:32.860
will damage the national
security of the United States.

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:35.190
In support of equating
John Bolton's disclosures

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:37.840
with an H-bomb, the DOJ
filed several declarations

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:39.100
from Ellis and other officials,

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:41.680
explaining that the
consequences of disclosure

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.330
would be quote, grave.

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:44.180
The Department of Justice

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:47.400
filed several classified
in-camera declarations

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:50.510
describing the supposedly
classified portions

00:18:50.510 --> 00:18:51.950
of Bolton's manuscript.

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:54.510
But they did not file a
declaration from Ellen Knight,

00:18:54.510 --> 00:18:57.040
the first official who
reviewed John Bolton's book

00:18:57.040 --> 00:18:59.810
and allegedly said that it
didn't contain any classified

00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:01.040
or prohibited information.

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:04.040
We don't have any testimony
from her under oath,

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:06.010
and this is telling.

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:07.690
That takes us to an interesting quirk

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:11.030
known as Mandatory
Declassification Review.

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:12.790
It's probably good in this case

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:14.860
to be skeptical of the
government's declaration

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:17.990
that all secrets pose grave
threats to national security,

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:19.630
regardless of whether the President

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:22.150
is Donald Trump or Joe
Biden or somebody else.

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:23.640
And in these circumstances,

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:26.100
courts should hold the
government to a very heavy burden

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:27.700
before restraining freedom of the press,

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:29.220
especially in a case like this,

00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:32.150
where the horse has already left the barn.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.840
And newspapers are already
publishing information

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:37.850
from Bolton's book and he's
already taped a TV interview.

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:39.350
- I don't think he's fit for office,

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:42.430
I don't think he has the
competence to carry out the job.

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:44.350
- And remember, if there's no secret,

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:46.930
there's generally no
justification for censorship,

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:50.050
putting aside the issue of
getting all of Bolton's profits.

00:19:50.050 --> 00:19:52.580
And this is just one of the
reasons why I personally,

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:53.413
through Legal Eagle,

00:19:53.413 --> 00:19:56.620
has filed for a Mandatory
Declassification Review

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:59.010
of the classified declarations
filed by the government

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:00.750
on June 17th.

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:03.780
Mandatory Declassification
Review, also known as MDR,

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:06.080
is a means by which any
individual or entity

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:08.260
can request any federal agency

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:11.390
to review classified information
for declassification,

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.300
subject to certain limitations.

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:15.380
The request has to describe the document

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:17.100
or material containing the information

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:19.830
with sufficient specificity
to enable the agency

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:22.230
to locate it with a
reasonable amount of effort.

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:25.640
And thankfully for us, the
DOJ has made that really easy,

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:27.200
since all the agency has to do

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.550
is go through the same
material that it just filed

00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:32.260
in support of the temporary
restraining order.

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:33.830
This will probably take some time

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:35.870
and could involve a lawsuit

00:20:35.870 --> 00:20:38.660
and an appeal of whatever
decision the DOJ makes,

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:41.660
but Legal Eagle is committed
to seeing this project through,

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:43.630
including through litigation.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.690
So if President Trump's administration

00:20:45.690 --> 00:20:47.550
is playing games with classification,

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:51.400
and there has been plenty of
indication of this in the past,

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:54.110
then I think we ought to know about it.

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:55.490
President Trump recently claimed

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:58.040
that every conversation
with him is classified.

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:01.740
- Even conversations with me,
they're highly classified,

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:03.630
I told that to the
Attorney General before.

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:05.500
I will consider every conversation

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:08.130
with me as President, highly classified.

00:21:08.130 --> 00:21:10.990
- And this is absolutely not
the way any of this works.

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:12.510
And as for what happens next,

00:21:12.510 --> 00:21:14.580
the court is going to
review the classifications

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.890
and determine if it had
good reason to classify

00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:19.440
and therefore censor
the material at issue.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:23.160
So with that background of
the entire John Bolton saga,

00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:25.940
let's talk about the
government's emergency motion

00:21:25.940 --> 00:21:27.680
for a temporary restraining order,

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:31.100
because we now know how this
at least preliminary portion

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:32.410
of this case ends.

00:21:32.410 --> 00:21:36.520
Now, a TRO is a court order
to do or not do something

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:37.900
for a short amount of time,

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:40.400
generally only for a
few days or a few weeks

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:42.040
until the court can have a full hearing

00:21:42.040 --> 00:21:44.100
on what's called the
preliminary injunction.

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:46.980
A preliminary injunction
is a similar order

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:48.060
that generally lasts

00:21:48.060 --> 00:21:51.590
throughout the entire length
of the particular case,

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:53.760
and at the end of the case,
there is a permanent order

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:57.270
that orders the parties to do
something or not do something.

00:21:57.270 --> 00:21:59.900
Now, a TRO, because it
is an emergency motion

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:02.080
with a very, very short timeline,

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:04.100
generally has the highest burden

00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:06.330
of all of those different injunctions.

00:22:06.330 --> 00:22:09.870
Because you don't get much
time to present evidence,

00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:12.700
you don't get much time
to show that things

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:14.140
are such an emergency

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:16.810
that they require this
temporary restraining order.

00:22:16.810 --> 00:22:19.590
So in order to get a TRO,
you need to do four things.

00:22:19.590 --> 00:22:20.423
You have to show, one,

00:22:20.423 --> 00:22:22.460
a substantial likelihood
of success on the merits,

00:22:22.460 --> 00:22:24.670
that means that you're
likely to win the case

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:27.150
when it actually gets to
the merits of the case.

00:22:27.150 --> 00:22:28.470
Number two, you have to show

00:22:28.470 --> 00:22:30.490
that you would suffer irreparable injury

00:22:30.490 --> 00:22:32.270
if the injunction is not granted.

00:22:32.270 --> 00:22:36.240
Now, generally, money damages
are not irreparable injury,

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:37.190
you have to show something

00:22:37.190 --> 00:22:40.000
that absolutely cannot
be properly compensated

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:42.270
in the absence of this injunction.

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:44.460
Number three, you have to
show that the injunction

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:47.200
will not substantially injure
other interested parties.

00:22:47.200 --> 00:22:49.820
And number four, you have to
prove that the public interest

00:22:49.820 --> 00:22:51.700
will be furthered by the injunction.

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:53.970
Now, that is a very, very high burden,

00:22:53.970 --> 00:22:56.760
especially on just a couple of days notice

00:22:56.760 --> 00:22:59.260
which is generally what
happens when you ask for a TRO.

00:22:59.260 --> 00:23:02.140
And here, the judge in this
particular case, Judge Lamberth,

00:23:02.140 --> 00:23:04.930
decided that the government
was likely to win

00:23:04.930 --> 00:23:06.450
on the NDA issue.

00:23:06.450 --> 00:23:08.650
The judge thought that it was likely,

00:23:08.650 --> 00:23:10.460
though certainly not certain,

00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:13.880
that John Bolton had published
classified information.

00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:15.680
And that was after an in-camera review,

00:23:15.680 --> 00:23:17.630
meaning that the court behind closed doors

00:23:17.630 --> 00:23:20.700
actually looked at the
evidence that was presented

00:23:20.700 --> 00:23:22.800
to the judge in this particular case,

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:23.650
and the judge thinks

00:23:23.650 --> 00:23:27.580
that Bolton probably published
classified information.

00:23:27.580 --> 00:23:30.570
The judge also found that
the NDAs prohibit disclosure

00:23:30.570 --> 00:23:32.320
of this kind of classified information

00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:36.780
and thinks that Bolton
likely violated those NDAs

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:38.980
by publishing his book.

00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:41.970
But that's just the
first factor of the TRO,

00:23:41.970 --> 00:23:43.820
that the government is likely to succeed

00:23:43.820 --> 00:23:46.580
on at least a portion of
the merits going forward.

00:23:46.580 --> 00:23:49.450
But a single factor
isn't enough to get a TRO

00:23:49.450 --> 00:23:51.830
and here, the judge went
on to the second factor

00:23:51.830 --> 00:23:52.940
and found that the government

00:23:52.940 --> 00:23:54.690
had not proved irreparable harm.

00:23:54.690 --> 00:23:57.670
In a case like this, the
information is already out there,

00:23:57.670 --> 00:23:59.440
the information has been published.

00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:00.550
The book is out there,

00:24:00.550 --> 00:24:03.110
it's in the hands of a
whole bunch of reviewers

00:24:03.110 --> 00:24:05.790
and the news media has access to the book,

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:07.770
you can get access to it.

00:24:07.770 --> 00:24:10.250
So because the information
is already out there,

00:24:10.250 --> 00:24:11.870
the harm has already occurred

00:24:11.870 --> 00:24:13.967
and an injunction isn't
going to solve anything

00:24:13.967 --> 00:24:16.910
and the government isn't likely
to suffer irreparable harm

00:24:16.910 --> 00:24:20.160
as a result of not granting a
temporary restraining order.

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:24.050
So the judge denied the TRO
and this case will go on,

00:24:24.050 --> 00:24:25.390
eventually there will be a hearing

00:24:25.390 --> 00:24:26.930
on the preliminary injunction

00:24:26.930 --> 00:24:28.570
and eventually there
will be a full hearing

00:24:28.570 --> 00:24:29.810
on the merits of the case,

00:24:29.810 --> 00:24:31.830
which is going to be a complicated trial

00:24:31.830 --> 00:24:36.830
about what John Bolton knew,
what information is classified,

00:24:37.030 --> 00:24:38.308
whether the information itself

00:24:38.308 --> 00:24:42.010
that Bolton included in his
book was classified or not.

00:24:42.010 --> 00:24:42.920
And interestingly,

00:24:42.920 --> 00:24:45.580
the judge specifically
left open the possibility

00:24:45.580 --> 00:24:47.660
of criminal charges against Bolton,

00:24:47.660 --> 00:24:51.164
the judge is not screwing
around in this particular case.

00:24:51.164 --> 00:24:54.400
So let's talk about those
potential criminal charges.

00:24:54.400 --> 00:24:57.530
Well, the restraining order
against Bolton is a civil case.

00:24:57.530 --> 00:24:59.640
He could in fact face criminal charges

00:24:59.640 --> 00:25:01.390
if the DOJ decides to prosecute him

00:25:01.390 --> 00:25:03.940
over the information he's
included in his book.

00:25:03.940 --> 00:25:06.620
There are many different
laws prohibiting mishandling

00:25:06.620 --> 00:25:08.180
or disclosure of classified material,

00:25:08.180 --> 00:25:11.447
for example, 18 USC 1924 which states,

00:25:11.447 --> 00:25:13.947
"Whoever being an officer,
employee, contractor

00:25:13.947 --> 00:25:15.657
"or consultant of the United States,

00:25:15.657 --> 00:25:16.967
"and by virtue of his office,

00:25:16.967 --> 00:25:19.617
"employment position or contract

00:25:19.617 --> 00:25:21.227
"becomes possessed of documents

00:25:21.227 --> 00:25:23.376
"or materials containing
classified information

00:25:23.376 --> 00:25:25.017
"of the United States,

00:25:25.017 --> 00:25:27.497
"knowingly removes such
documents or materials

00:25:27.497 --> 00:25:29.397
"without authority and with the intent

00:25:29.397 --> 00:25:31.737
"to retain such documents or materials

00:25:31.737 --> 00:25:35.427
"at an unauthorized location
shall be fined under this title

00:25:35.427 --> 00:25:39.050
"or imprisoned for not more
than five years or both."

00:25:39.050 --> 00:25:40.960
And this has happened before.

00:25:40.960 --> 00:25:42.950
Former CIA Director, David Petraeus,

00:25:42.950 --> 00:25:45.170
pleaded guilty to mishandling
classified information

00:25:45.170 --> 00:25:47.950
simply because he gave
it to his biographer,

00:25:47.950 --> 00:25:50.910
even though she didn't use
the information in his book.

00:25:50.910 --> 00:25:53.070
And Bolton made a major faux pas

00:25:53.070 --> 00:25:55.670
in how he dealt with the
pre-publication process,

00:25:55.670 --> 00:25:56.910
because the government's complaint

00:25:56.910 --> 00:25:59.910
alleges that Bolton violated
his obligations under the NDAs

00:25:59.910 --> 00:26:02.950
by sharing classified
information, quote, numerous times

00:26:02.950 --> 00:26:05.140
before his book was published and printed,

00:26:05.140 --> 00:26:07.410
just by discussing it with his lawyer,

00:26:07.410 --> 00:26:09.860
publisher and members of the news media.

00:26:09.860 --> 00:26:12.610
It's kind of crazy that these laws exist,

00:26:12.610 --> 00:26:15.630
but those laws do exist.

00:26:15.630 --> 00:26:16.463
And publication

00:26:16.463 --> 00:26:19.010
can mean giving potentially
classified information

00:26:19.010 --> 00:26:23.180
to anyone the government has
not pre-approved to receive it.

00:26:23.180 --> 00:26:26.720
And Bolton's lawyer admitted
to reviewing the information

00:26:26.720 --> 00:26:29.700
in an article that he wrote
for various newspapers.

00:26:29.700 --> 00:26:33.430
And the NDAs don't allow Bolton
to share classified material

00:26:33.430 --> 00:26:35.920
with anyone, not a publisher,
not a lawyer, not as friends

00:26:35.920 --> 00:26:36.950
and not the media.

00:26:36.950 --> 00:26:40.590
So in this case, what
should Bolton have done?

00:26:40.590 --> 00:26:42.250
Well, we're going to find out

00:26:42.250 --> 00:26:44.440
and I'm actually going
to make sure of that

00:26:44.440 --> 00:26:45.760
because this is the first time

00:26:45.760 --> 00:26:48.520
that Legal Eagle is
branching out into activism.

00:26:48.520 --> 00:26:50.810
Because these are unprecedented times

00:26:50.810 --> 00:26:54.380
and the information that Bolton
knows and tried to publish

00:26:54.380 --> 00:26:57.520
may strike at the heart
of the impeachment trial

00:26:57.520 --> 00:27:00.410
and what President Trump
was accused of doing

00:27:00.410 --> 00:27:03.774
with respect to potentially
using taxpayer money

00:27:03.774 --> 00:27:06.050
in order to extort a foreign power

00:27:06.050 --> 00:27:07.970
to help him in an election.

00:27:07.970 --> 00:27:10.390
And because this is so important,

00:27:10.390 --> 00:27:12.800
Legal Eagle filed FOIA
request with the government

00:27:12.800 --> 00:27:15.340
and the government has
so far stonewalled us,

00:27:15.340 --> 00:27:19.060
which has caused us to file
